Pursue **Project 1: Minimizing the entropy of language-model outputs.**

It represents the ideal research project profile: it is built on a clear, compelling hypothesis, has a well-defined and feasible execution plan, is de-risked by its modular components, and its success would constitute a significant and practical contribution to improving LLM reasoning.

You can frame your paper as a comprehensive investigation into entropy as a key lever for improving model confidence and correctness in logical tasks. The three-part structure (FT, RL, INF) makes for a very strong and complete narrative.

**A Potential Future Path:** Success in Project 1 could even lay the groundwork for a better version of Project 2. A model fine-tuned with EM-RL could serve as a much better "System 2" base model for future model-merging experiments. You're not abandoning the exciting ideas of Project 2, but rather building the rigorous foundation necessary to tackle them later.
